  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000121570,
      "SummaryText": "Sun Cosmetics LLC owned by Sun Chemical Corp is a manufacturer of synthetic iron oxides for cosmetic grade color pigments and magnetic storage media. One of the raw materials used in this process is agricultural grade anhydrous ammonia (anhydrous means without water). Approximately 80% of all ammonia produced is used in agriculture as a nitrogen source for corn and a protein source in livestock feeds. Other common uses for ammonia are metal treating, pharmaceuticals, synthetic textile fibers, plastics, water treatment and commercial refrigeration systems. Anhydrous Ammonia is classified as a flammable gas with a reportable spill quantity of 100 pounds. Sun Cosmetics uses detailed procedures and employee training to maintain the safe operation of this system. Detection sensors are strategically located to alert personnel of leaks. Remotely operated shut off valves, internal tank automatic isolation valves, and a remotely operated water deluge system minimizes the effect of a failed component. Sun Cosmetics participates in the Local Emergency Planning Commission (LEPC) and invites the local Fire Department and Hazardous Materials Response Team to train on site. Our internal emergency response plan includes coordinating with police, fire, and HAZMAT personnel. Sun has had no reportable releases or injuries from ammonia in the last 15 years. Sun is committed to operating this system in a safe and responsible manor, protecting our employees and the surrounding community.\n\nAccess to the outdoor ammonia storage tank system is controlled with an 8-foot tall chain link fence topped with barbed wire and locked gates. This is along with the entire site being within the security fenced and gated around the perimeter of the facility. We also have a system of HD cameras on DVR that monitor all facility access points and the ammonia tank storage area. \n\nEarlier this year, a new precipitation reactor was brought online for testing and verification. This reactor has upgraded control"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000121570,
      "SummaryText": "s, interlocks, piping, and a few additional items that our legacy reactors do not. Testing the effectiveness of the upgraded system will be a step process, but each item will be verified to ensure it is appropriate for our process. With the addition of this reactor, two legacy reactors have been removed from service due to their end of life and cost to maintain.\n\nA new Sun Chemical anhydrous ammonia specific piping specification has been established and implemented across the ammonia tank, piping, and reactors. Essentially all piping, valves, and controls have been replaced and/or upgraded to ensure proper design. \n\nThe January 2020 RMP regulatory inspection is ongoing with hopes that it will wrap up through a CAFO later this year."
    }
  ]
